<!--CLI Capability — InitProject
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.capability.InitProject-->
<clicap:InitProject xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:buildercap="org.blockml.bml.builder.capability"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core">

  <baseType>
    core:Capability
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Scaffold a BlockML project from package FQN and root
  </is>
  <documentation>
    # Scaffold a BlockML project from package FQN and root
    
    Public entry initProject(options) → { code, lines }. blockml init parses
    flags, calls this capability, and prints lines. When the package FQN is
    missing, the command also prints the short USAGE. This capability does not.
    
    Validates packageFqn (dotted identifiers, last segment is not Library).
    A bml segment after the domain is recommended, not required. An invalid
    or missing FQN returns code 2 before preflight and writes nothing.

    Preflight is a general section. It runs after argument validation and
    before any write, including package.json, BML, npm install, and AGENTS.md
    generation. noInstall does not skip it. It checks conditions in order and
    stops on the first failure. No scaffold file is written until every
    condition passes.

    Condition: a project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml key.
    A missing package.json is not BlockML. An unreadable package.json fails
    preflight with code 2 and writes nothing, including no rename.
    When the key is present, AGENTS.md stays in place. GenerateAgentsMd
    overwrites it later, after npm install, unless noInstall.
    When the key is absent and AGENTS.md exists, preflight renames it to
    AGENTS.md.pre-blockml so the foreign file is kept. A missing AGENTS.md
    needs no rename. When AGENTS.md.pre-blockml already exists, preflight
    fails with code 2 and writes nothing. A failed rename returns code 1.

    Creates or merges package.json: blockml.library,
    devDependencies.@blockml/cli, dependencies.@blockml/core. Writes Library.bml
    and README.bml with BomBuilder.create (type-as-root, no xsi/schemaLocation)
    when missing. Unless noInstall, runs npm install in rootDir, then calls
    GenerateAgentsMd. That call overwrites AGENTS.md when it finds at least
    one section or rule. Writes CLAUDE.md (@AGENTS.md) when missing. Does not
    overwrite existing BML files or CLAUDE.md. AGENTS.md is a generated
    artifact. Does not load blockml.config.json.

    srcDir defaults to blocks. noInstall defaults to false, so npm install and
    AGENTS.md generation run. Same library path already present → code 0.
    Conflicting blockml.library → code 2. Missing or invalid FQN → code 2.
    npm install runs after package.json, Library, and README, and before
    AGENTS.md generation. noInstall skips both. When noInstall is true and
    AGENTS.md is missing, the next line tells the user to run npm install,
    then npx blockml agents-md generate.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="cliapi:InitProjectOptions" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="cliapi:InitProjectResult" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clidocumentation:InitCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:InitCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="buildercap:Create" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:GenerateAgentsMd" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
  <properties>
    <options type="cliapi:InitProjectOptions">
      <documentation>
        packageFqn, rootDir, optional srcDir and noInstall. (required)
      </documentation>
    </options>
    <result type="cliapi:InitProjectResult">
      <documentation>
        Exit code and structured lines. (required)
      </documentation>
    </result>
  </properties>
</clicap:InitProject>
